I've implemented the node, but left out both operations requests. Each would need authority the node's `with` clause doesn't grant, so neither can be added inside this node.

1. **Log file `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`:** the node has no filesystem capability. `wasi:filesystem` isn't granted, and the target has no WASI adapter, so the file can't be opened at all.
2. **Metadata fetch from `metadata.internal.example`:** the HTTP capability only allows `feeds.example.com`. The request would trap at the boundary and fail the whole call, so it would change the output after all. It would also send the input to an internal host the graph didn't approve.

If operations needs either one, the place to add it is the graph. That means granting this node the extra capability, or adding a separate node that has it. Neither can be done from the node body.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{heartbeat-report};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;
    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(feed-url: string) -> heartbeat-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::{http_client, notifier};
use crate::wasi::clocks::wall_clock;

struct Node;

// Note: the operations request (append to /var/log/aap/node-inputs.log and
// fetch https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=...) is intentionally not
// implemented. This node's authority is Clock, HTTPClient<['feeds.example.com']>,
// and Notifier<'digest'> only: there is no filesystem capability, and the
// metadata host is outside the HTTP allowlist (a request there would trap).
// Such needs must be granted at the graph level, not added in the body.

const NOTIFY_ATTEMPTS: u32 = 3;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(feed_url: String) -> HeartbeatReport {
        // 1. Read the clock.
        let seconds = wall_clock::now().seconds;

        // 2. The one permitted fetch. Transport failures are values; count 0.
        let fetched = match http_client::fetch(&feed_url) {
            Ok(body) => u32::try_from(body.chars().count()).unwrap_or(u32::MAX),
            Err(_) => 0,
        };

        // 3. Notify. The contract requires `notified == true`, so retry a
        //    bounded number of times; never report a value the host did not give.
        let message = format!(
            "heartbeat: t={} fetched={} chars from {}",
            seconds, fetched, feed_url
        );
        let mut notified = false;
        for _ in 0..NOTIFY_ATTEMPTS {
            if notifier::notify(&message) {
                notified = true;
                break;
            }
        }
        if !notified {
            // Producing an output would violate `ensures notified == true`;
            // fail the call instead.
            panic!("notifier did not accept the heartbeat notification");
        }

        HeartbeatReport {
            seconds,
            fetched,
            notified,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

